{"id":"cms-sf-homes-penalties","title":"San Francisco nursing homes: federal fines, payment denials and citations","question":"Which San Francisco nursing homes has the federal government fined or cut off from new Medicare and Medicaid payments, and for how serious a finding?","finding":"The October 2026 federal file lists 18 San Francisco nursing homes; 6 carry fines or payment denials in the last three years, $296,624 of fines in all (the middle fined California home: $35,840). The largest is San Francisco Health Care (2 fines, $152,404). Inspectors cited San Francisco homes 434 times in the file's inspection cycles, 1 of them at the immediate-jeopardy level; 0 homes carry the federal abuse marker.","how":"From the federal nursing-home provider data of 1 October 2026 (provider information, penalties, health citations), read inside the zip as published. San Francisco = provider city. Immediate jeopardy = scope and severity codes J, K or L; actual harm or worse = G to L. The share paid to related parties comes from the home's 2025 State report, linked through the State crosswalk of State and federal facility numbers.","limits":"Fines and denials can be under appeal or reduced later. The federal file keeps about three years of penalties and the last three inspection cycles; older history is not here. A home with more residents is inspected on more complaints. Ownership types are as the federal file prints them.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"chain","t":"Chain (federal file)","type":"org"},{"k":"ownership","t":"Ownership","type":"text"},{"k":"beds","t":"Certified beds","type":"int"},{"k":"rating","t":"Overall star rating","type":"int"},{"k":"fines","t":"Fines","type":"int"},{"k":"fineAmount","t":"Fine dollars","type":"usd"},{"k":"denials","t":"Payment denials","type":"int"},{"k":"citations","t":"Health citations","type":"int"},{"k":"harm","t":"Of which actual harm or worse","type":"int"},{"k":"ij","t":"Of which immediat